\f0\fs26 \cf0 The door was a pristine slab of stone amid the craggy rock of the cave. Wildly out of place, it dominated this side of the lake despite it\'92s normal dimensions. It was tall, but not hugely so, and wide, but no more than some doorways in his own palace. It was a door for men, or more probably for elves. Markal stood before it, one hand outstretched, hesitant to touch that alien surface.\
Around him stood the rest of his mismatched group, all full again having breakfasted on more of the odd fish and crab creatures. They were content to let him be the one to open the door. In fact Peter had taken the precaution of going all the way to the water line, from where he watched, arms crossed, in apprehension.\
\'93Come on, push it. We\'92re ready,\'94 said Liesbet. She adjusted her grip on the hammer she had raised ready.\
