\i \cf0 What is this place?
\i0  Markal asked.\

\i It is the College of the Way. This is where the Aelfin came to study the holes between our world and yours.\
I thought the breaches were in Eranor. The Aelfin came to Duranor from Eranor and found us here. They didn\'92t come through here, did they?\
No, originally they came through what you call the Ridge in Eranor, but the holes are everywhere. Wherever you find the fabric of the world, you will find gaps, pathways, portals. The worlds are inextricably joined by their cores.\
Stone? The fabric of the world, the bedrock. That\'92s why they came through the Ridge. The mountains, all that stone reaching up from beneath the surface\'85 
\i0 Markal gasped audibly, causing Liesbet to give him a quizzical look. He just smiled at her.\

\i Yes. Wherever you find enough stone. Real, connected, core stone, you\'92ll find cracks. Here, under Duranor, there are just as many as you\'92ll find under the Ridge. They shift, they go dormant for years at a time, new ones pop up from time to time, but there\'92s always that link.\
